Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:11:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 41/44] drama: a stream's silence guard hears each chunk before
 handing it over, and both paths cut at the same frame

On our GB10, our corpus, a collapsing reply in a model-invented test voice now ends at 16.579 s streamed and whole, with identical PCM; before, the stream ran 29.77 s against 17.09 s whole, the 12.7 s in the changelog. The 46 normal default-voice corpus replies stayed byte-identical and streams passed 9 of 9.
